## .STATUS Parser Hardening (2026-07-16, PR #87 MERGED): `StatusFileParser` now warns (not silently swallows) on non-numeric `progress:` values and duplicate top-level keys — value extraction unchanged from prior `parseInt` behavior (verified via dogfood against `~/projects/research`, no regressions). Warnings surface via `atlas sync --from-status`/`--research` and `atlas doctor` (opt-in `statusFileParser` injection). Spec: `docs/specs/SPEC-status-parser-hardening-2026-07-16.md`. Dogfood run surfaced 6 research repos with genuine pre-existing duplicate-key noise — all fixed, 5 PRs open against `draft` (interventional-mediation#1, path-specific-mediation#1, medbounds#1, mult_med#1, sensitivity#1) + pmed-modern#15 (real correctness fix: progress 92%→89%, a stale 6-week-old snapshot was silently shadowing the current header). **Held for user to merge** — not merged by this session per explicit instruction.

## Quick Context
Atlas is the project state engine - a standalone Node.js package providing
Clean Architecture-based state management for developer workflows. Designed
with ADHD-friendly features like streak tracking and celebration helpers.

